Ownership
(Signal 01: Fix, Guide & Tidy Up)

Diagnostic Scope: Evaluates whether the advisor
strongly owned the path forward and managed
escalations with full transparency, regardless of
the outcome

Behaviors To Look For: The advisor takes end-to-
end accountability. They provide total

transparency on steps and escalations, ensure
clean wrap-up, and deliver long-term strategic
guidance for merchant growth.

• Deflects responsibility or leaves next steps
ambiguous; provides no clear escalation
timelines; closes prematurely without verifying
resolution
• Passes burden to merchant, policy, Shopify,
another team, or a third party
• Escalation Follow-ups: Frames status as
"nothing I can do" or "you just have to wait"
instead of actively guiding the status and next
steps

• States clear accountability, sets exact
expectations for paths/escalations, and delivers a
complete, concise wrap-up
• Advisor provides a path forward, though without
strongly owning or deeply detailing the end-to-end
journey

• Elevates from transactional problem-solver to
consultative business partner. Total accountability
extends to long-term success with tailored, strategic
guidance
• Escalation Standards: Confidently explains existing path,
confirms merchant is in the right process, and clarifies
where response originates without implying support can
force or speed up external processes

Lower Merchant Effort
(Signal 02: Research & Align)

Diagnostic Scope: Evaluates how much
unnecessary work the merchant had to do to move
the issue forward.
Behaviors To Look For: The advisor eliminates
cognitive friction and repetition. They Proactively
investigate ticket history, store configuration, and
logs to execute solutions directly without
burdening the merchant.

• Asks merchant to repeat details already
provided; shifts manual troubleshooting
burden onto user; offers generic links instead
of direct resolution
• Merchant had to chase, search, interpret,
figure out next steps alone, or navigate
complex technical jargon without guidance
• Advisor provides too many steps at once
without matching merchant skill level

• Reviews tickets, achieves zero repetition of prior
inputs, and executes actions directly on the user's
behalf
• Merchant had to take reasonable, appropriate
steps that were clearly and concisely explained
• Calibration Guardrail: Do not penalize advisors if
the merchant was asked to take reasonable,
clearly explained steps.

• Preemptive resolution: Proactively mines history and logs
to identify and independently resolve downstream or
chronic issues before they impact the merchant
• Absorbs 100% of cognitive and technical heavy lifting by
using available context, direct paths, clear instructions, or
executing the work directly
• Observable Evidence: Merchant reacts to unexpected,
unprompted value (e.g., "I didn't even realize my shipping
zones were broken too, thank you for fixing that before it
became a problem!").

Genuine Empathy
(Signal 03: Connect First)

Diagnostic Scope: Evaluates whether the advisor
acknowledged the merchant's situation in a useful,
specific, human, and tailored way
Behaviors To Look For: The advisor connects with
the merchant as a person before and during the
interaction. They validate emotional reality,
express authentic human care, and align urgency
with immediate action.
Note: Using standard call center empathy spiels
without the human connection does not equate to
Genuine Empathy.

• Fails to acknowledge distress, context, or
emotional reality; uses canned, dismissive, or
robotic scripts without warmth
• Empty empathy, bluntness, negative
mirroring, policy-blaming, or lack of human
communication
• Calibration Guardrail: Do not mark empathy
as "Does Not Meet Expectations" solely
because merchant sentiment or survey rating
was negative.

• Agent validates the real situation directly, pairs
warmth with immediate action, and uses an
authentic, non-robotic tone.
• Polite, respectful, and acknowledges the
situation, though not deeply personalized or
situational.

• Shifts from situational to deeply personal and impactful
empathy. Reverses a highly negative or stressed
emotional state by recognizing the true business stakes.
• Specific acknowledgment tied directly to the merchant's
actual issue and impact.
• Calibration Guardrail: Generic phrases (e.g., "I completely
understand", "I know how important this is") do NOT
qualify as "Exceeds Expectations" unless paired with
specific acknowledgment and immediate action.
• Observable Evidence: Merchant explicitly expresses
profound relief or renewed trust (e.g., "I was having a panic
attack about this launch, you completely saved the day!").






















